    {
      "id": "results",
      "title": "What the run established",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "The timing tool verified that its own mappings stayed locked and the target range stayed unlocked. Neither run lost or missed a probe. One run per kernel shows the measurement path works and leaves the speed difference unmeasured."
        },
        {
          "type": "bars",
          "takeaway": "Every timed read had a verified decompression",
          "categories": [
            "Original kernel",
            "Shared-library kernel"
          ],
          "series": [
            "Timed pages",
            "Verified decodes"
          ],
          "values": {
            "Timed pages": [
              32768,
              32768
            ],
            "Verified decodes": [
              32768,
              32768
            ]
          },
          "y_label": "Pages"
        }
      ],
      "lead": "The old timing tool saw two decoder returns for one timed access. With the tool's own memory pinned, the baseline and the shared-library kernel each completed the sequential and shuffled reads with full data checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "next",
      "title": "What remains to test",
      "lead": "The full comparison needs repeated calibration plus matched runs for the compressed and physical paths. It needs more guest attempts than remain in the original budget.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "Independent XSwap still needs its guest driver and physical-path validation. A platform review interrupted the driver work. The pressure-driven migration test starts after independent XSwap passes correctness."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "patches",
      "title": "Core kernel patches",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "diff",
          "takeaway": "Free compressed objects through the shared library",
          "patch": "diff --git a/mm/zswap.c b/mm/zswap.c\nindex 789730c22..e5b93c7da 100644\n--- a/mm/zswap.c\n+++ b/mm/zswap.c\n@@ -780,7 +693,7 @@ static void zswap_entry_free(struct zswap_entry *entry)\n \n \tzswap_lru_del(entry);\n \tif (!WARN_ON_ONCE(!pool)) {\n-\t\tzs_free(pool->zs_pool, entry->handle);\n+\t\tpage_compress_free(pool->compress, entry->handle);\n \t\tzswap_pool_put(pool);\n \t}\n \tif (entry->objcg) {\n"
        }
      ]
    },
